<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/intensionextension.owl#"
     xml:base="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/intensionextension.owl"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:cpannotationschema="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#"
     xmlns:intensionextension="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/intensionextension.owl#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/intensionextension.owl">
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl"/>
        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To represent the meaning of an information object: the concepts it expresses, the things it is about.</dcterms:description>
        <dcterms:title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Intensionextension Pattern</dcterms:title>
        <cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>What is the meaning of an information object?,What information objects express this meaning?,What is this about?,How can I call this?</cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>
        <cpannotationschema:extractedFrom>http://ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl</cpannotationschema:extractedFrom>
        <cpannotationschema:extractedFrom>http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl</cpannotationschema:extractedFrom>
        <cpannotationschema:hasAuthor>Aldo Gangemi and Valentina Presutti</cpannotationschema:hasAuthor>
        <cpannotationschema:hasConsequences>We are able to distinguish between the intension of the meaning of an information object (its social object, e.g. a concept), and its extension (the entities or ets of entities it can be about).
In practice, this pattern allows to encode a minimal version of the semiotic triangle, and it&apos;s useful in all cases where the domain and task need to represent in a same ontology e.g. eords, concepts, and things.
SKOS has an overlap with this pattern.</cpannotationschema:hasConsequences>
        <cpannotationschema:hasIntent rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To represent the meaning of an information object: the concepts it expresses, the things it is about.</cpannotationschema:hasIntent>
        <cpannotationschema:hasUnitTest>SELECT ?m
WHERE {
?e :expresses ?m}

SELECT ?t
WHERE {
?e :isAbout ?t}

</cpannotationschema:hasUnitTest>
        <cpannotationschema:relatedCPs>InformationRealization,LMM,Tagging,Topic</cpannotationschema:relatedCPs>
        <cpannotationschema:scenarios>&apos;Leonardo da Vinci&apos; is the name of the main Rome airport,&apos;Legal Person&apos; means an incorporated entity with legal status.</cpannotationschema:scenarios>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK&apos;s quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label moved to skos:prefLabel x6; label added x11; term declared x3;
- header: dcterms:title &quot;Intensionextension Pattern&quot; - the library&apos;s name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library&apos;s description of the pattern
Each change is listed under &quot;curated&quot; in the pattern&apos;s metadata.json in OntoBoard&apos;s pattern library.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>The intension and extension pattern. It allows to represent the intensional expression and extensional reference of information objects. This pattern is extracted from DOLCE-UltraLite by partial clone of elements.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>intension extension</rdfs:label>
        <owl:versionInfo>1.1
- Added annotation for ODP publication
1.0
- Created by Aldo Gangemi and Valentina Presutti</owl:versionInfo>
        <owl:versionInfo rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.1 added rdfs:isDefinedBy for all named entities</owl:versionInfo>
        <owl:versionInfo rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Created by Valentina Presutti and Aldo Gangemi</owl:versionInfo>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


